   "source": [
    "# Reversed Sentiment Analysis â€” multi-company version\n",
    "\n",
    "Extends the original single-company (SABIC) notebook to run the same *reversed sentiment* pipeline over\n",
    "every company in `Companies.csv`, using one news file (`AllNews.csv`, company-tagged, timestamped) and one\n",
    "price file (`StockPrices.csv`, all companies).\n",
    "\n",
    "What changed relative to the original notebook (each item is marked `# CHANGED` in the code):\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Multi-company loop** â€” the pipeline is wrapped in functions and run per `CompanyID`; a pooled (all-company) lexicon is also built.\n",
    "2. **New input schemas** â€” `StockPrices.csv` has no header; columns are mapped explicitly. News is joined on `CompanyID`.\n",
    "3. **Timestamps â†’ trading-day alignment** â€” headlines published after the session opens are assigned to the *next* trading day\n",
    "   (`ALIGNMENT = \"next_session\"`). The original same-day behaviour is still available (`ALIGNMENT = \"same_day\"`).\n",
    "4. **Returns instead of `Close âˆ’ Open`** â€” configurable `TARGET` (`oc_log`, `cc_log`, or the original `diff`).\n",
    "5. **Chronological train/test split by date** (`TRAIN_END`), identical for every company.\n",
    "6. **Light Arabic normalisation + minimum word frequency** so that `\"Ø³Ø§Ø¨Ùƒ\"`, `Ø³Ø§Ø¨Ùƒ` and `Ø³Ø§Ø¨Ùƒ.` are one token.\n",
    "7. **Daily score computed as the documented sum** (the original code used a mean and silently dropped unmatched words).\n",
    "8. **Evaluation table**: same-day and next-day correlation with p-values, directional accuracy, balanced accuracy and the\n",
    "   majority-class baseline, for every company.\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything is controlled from the `CONFIG` cell."
   ]
  },
